{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For there is no divination in Jacob.</b> Since the King's trumpet-blast is in him and he has cleaving to HaShem, they will not need diviners and soothsayers, for at every time He will declare to Israel in prophecy what El will do, for all His deeds are decreed from the outset." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> 'At that time it will be said to Jacob and Israel, what' — at that time of which it is said (Daniel 12:1) ״ובעת ההוא יעמוד מיכאל השר הגדול״ and so forth — He will say to Jacob and Israel: 'How great is Your goodness that You have laid up for those who fear You' (Psalms 31:20), and it is written (Isaiah 23:18) ״כי ליושבים לפני ה׳ יהיה סחרה״ and so forth."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:31.235597621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}